Verified before closing out: `npm run build` succeeds full monorepo (frontend static export + backend bundle); `/ad-min` CMS logs in and renders correctly in the new tokens (admin@teww.local / password in frontend/.env CMS_ADMIN_PASSWORD), fully isolated from the public redesign; all 7 public pages clean at 390px mobile width.

Gotcha for next time: editing `frontend/data/seed.json` does NOT update the live site — it only seeds the DB via `npm run db:seed` (upsert, safe to rerun), and Next's fetch cache (tag `site-content`) needs the frontend process restarted to pick up a reseed done outside the CMS publish flow. Also: never re-serialize seed.json with `json.dump`/indent — reformats the whole file; always use targeted Edit insertions like [[heard-redesign]]'s en.json approach.

Local stack: postgres in docker `teww-pg` (port 5433, colima; DOCKER_HOST=unix://$HOME/.colima/default/docker.sock), env in frontend/.env + backend/.env, `npm run dev` = frontend :3000 + backend :3001. Pollinations MCP is flaky under parallel calls (max 1 concurrent anonymous request) — go sequential with ~8s gaps, or use generateImage then re-fetch via curl to image.pollinations.ai if the MCP result isn't saved to disk.
